# Build the Bare Page

## Step

Paste a URL, see the report with per-state flags, contact CTA placeholder.

## Result (2026-11-03)

Done on stage `dev`: the Foldkit page in `apps/web` takes a URL, follows the scan, shows the report with per-state applicability and flags, and has the contact form (builder-cloud for the page, scan views and contact form; builder-core redesigned the report view). The website Worker forwards `/rpc` to the Scanner over its service binding. It rate-limits `startScan` and `sendMessage` per caller (IPv4 address or IPv6 /64), takes POST only, and passes the caller key to the per-site daily cap (`docs/layer-2-3.md`).

Left:
- Review R6 is done (49d240b): `/report/<site>/<scan ID>` shows that scan, and `/report/<site>` the newest.
- Turnstile stays deferred (decision 14). The rate limit binding is approximate, so the global daily caps remain the real ceiling.
